@startuml
title Proposed isolated issue-job boundary
participant "Control plane" as CP
participant "Trusted supervisor" as SUP
participant "Disposable job guest" as GUEST
participant "Host egress proxy" as PROXY
participant "Model provider" as PROVIDER
participant "GitHub" as GH
database "Checkpoint store" as STORE

note over CP,SUP
  Proposed design; no new boundary control is claimed in place.
  Issue and repository content are untrusted.
end note
CP -> SUP: claim + stage + revision + fencing token + issue data
SUP -> SUP: validate policy, image, empty mounts, and grants
SUP -> GUEST: authenticated bounded job envelope
note over SUP,GUEST
  Trust boundary: guest cannot see supervisor credentials,
  host files, sibling checkouts, or other worker processes.
end note
SUP -> PROXY: grant job and fencing token for selected destinations
SUP -> GUEST: selected provider and active-repository grants
GUEST -> PROXY: provider request with job grant
PROXY -> PROVIDER: approved provider traffic
GUEST -> PROXY: active-repository GitHub operation
PROXY -> GH: approved repository traffic
GUEST -> SUP: untrusted result + checkout revision + checkpoint bytes
SUP -> SUP: validate schema, size, lineage, and claim fence
SUP -> STORE: opaque checkpoint + digest + retention deadline
SUP -> CP: fenced completion + trusted isolation record
SUP -> PROXY: revoke grant before replacement claim
SUP -> GUEST: terminate entire VM and descendants
note over SUP,STORE
  On retry, restore only into a fresh matching guest;
  never extract or execute checkpoint data on supervisor.
end note
@enduml
